  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Eldest hand leads. On each trick, a player who has led suit may either follow suit or play trump; if unable to follow suit they may play any card. If any trump is played, highest trump wins; otherwise highest card of led suit wins. Winner leads next. Cards remain face up in front of each player in play order. Three figures are scored each deal: Gleich (best set of equal ranks), Hanger (best suited sequence), and Spiel (team that wins at least 3 of 5 tricks). Betting on each figure can happen during play and can be conceded, seen, or raised. Play stops immediately when Spiel is decided or conceded, and unresolved Gleich/Hanger are settled by staged showdown reveals.',
    Player: 'Eldest hand leads. On each trick, a player who has led suit may either follow suit or play trump; if unable to follow suit they may play any card. If any trump is played, highest trump wins; otherwise highest card of led suit wins. Winner leads next. Cards remain face up in front of each player in play order. Three figures are scored each deal: Gleich (best set of equal ranks), Hanger (best suited sequence), and Spiel (team that wins at least 3 of 5 tricks). Betting on each figure can happen during play and can be conceded, seen, or raised. Play stops immediately when Spiel is decided or conceded, and unresolved Gleich/Hanger are settled by staged showdown reveals.',
    objective: 'Be the first partnership to reach the agreed target (usually 11 or 15 points).',
    gameplay: 'Eldest hand leads. On each trick, a player who has led suit may either follow suit or play trump; if unable to follow suit they may play any card. If any trump is played, highest trump wins; otherwise highest card of led suit wins. Winner leads next. Cards remain face up in front of each player in play order. Three figures are scored each deal: Gleich (best set of equal ranks), Hanger (best suited sequence), and Spiel (team that wins at least 3 of 5 tricks). Betting on each figure can happen during play and can be conceded, seen, or raised. Play stops immediately when Spiel is decided or conceded, and unresolved Gleich/Hanger are settled by staged showdown reveals.',
    keyRules: [
      'Initial value of each figure is 1 point and can be increased by accepted bets.',
      'Bets on a figure alternate by team; a team that just had its bet seen cannot bet that figure again until the other team bets it.',
      'Any player who bet or saw Gleich or Hanger must later prove they hold at least a minimal valid instance of that figure or incur penalty.',
      'When Spiel is decided early, trick play stops immediately and showdown begins for unresolved figures.',
    ],
