      'Turn-flow example: Eldest hand leads. On each trick, a player who has led suit may either follow suit or play trump; if unable to follow suit they may play any card. If any trump is played, highest trump wins; otherwise highest card of led suit wins. Winner leads next. Cards remain face up in front of each player in play order. Three figures are scored each deal: Gleich (best set of equal ranks), Hanger (best suited sequence), and Spiel (team that wins at least 3 of 5 tricks). Betting on each figure can happen during play and can be conceded, seen, or raised. Play stops immediately when Spiel is decided or conceded, and unresolved Gleich/Hanger are settled by staged showdown reveals.',
      'Scoring example: Each deal awards figure values for Gleich, Hanger, and Spiel, with values increased by accepted bets and modified by concessions or penalties. First partnership to reach agreed target score (typically 11 or 15) wins..',
